# WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION

REGENT OF BUOL

CENTRAL SULAWESI PROVINCE

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF BUOL REGENCY

NUMBER 07 OF 2018

CONCERNING

WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF BUOL,

Considering:







a. that every citizen has equal rights to live a dignified life in accordance with the principles of humanity, equality, and justice;
b. that to guarantee women's empowerment and child protection in accordance with human dignity and to receive protection from violence, discrimination and other violations, women's empowerment and child protection must be carried out in an integrated, continuous manner through the acceleration of fulfillment and protection of the rights of women and children in their personal lives, family, community, nation and state;
c. that in accordance with the provisions of Article 12 paragraph (2) letter b of Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 2014 concerning Regional Government, women's empowerment and child protection is one of the mandatory government affairs that is the authority of the Regional Government;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

In View of:







1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 51 of 1999 concerning the Establishment of Buol Regency, Morowali Regency, and Banggai Kepulauan Regency (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 179, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3900) as amended by Law Number 11 of 2000 concerning Amendment to Law Number 51 of 1999 concerning the Establishment of Buol Regency, Morowali Regency, and Banggai Kepulauan Regency (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2000 Number 78, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3966);
3. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);
4. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
5. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;
6. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2010 Number 446);
7. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2011 concerning National Socio-Cultural Strategy to realize Gender Equality (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 168);
8. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 11 of 2011 concerning Policy for the Development of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 168);
9. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 12 of 2011 concerning Indicators of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 169);
10. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 13 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for the Development of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 168);
11. Regulation of the Minister of Social Affairs Number 16 of 2013 concerning Family Welfare Consultation Institutions (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2013 Number 1509);
12. Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 6 of 2015 concerning the System of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 615);

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BUOL REGENCY

and

REGENT OF BUOL

DECIDES:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION.

